<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>Privacy Policy for RetroN VintageCam</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: December 2025</p>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>1. Developer Information</h2>
        <p>Developer: <strong>Elif Nida Kayaduman</strong><br />
        Contact Email: <a href="mailto:elifnida@gmail.com">elifnida@gmail.com</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>2. Overview</h2>
        <p>RetroN VintageCam is a retro-style camera and photo editing app. All image processing happens locally on your device. We do not operate servers and we do not collect, store, or transmit personal data.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>3. Information Processed Locally</h2>
        <p>The app processes only the following information, and only on your device:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Photos you select or capture</li>
            <li>Filters, frames, and effects you apply</li>
            <li>Optional custom date stamps</li>
            <li>Optional city/area label (if location permission is granted)</li>
            <li>Locally saved Memories metadata</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No information is transmitted to external servers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>4. Permissions</h2>
        <p>The app may request access to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Photos:</strong> To select and save edited images.</li>
            <li><strong>Camera:</strong> To capture photos inside the app.</li>
            <li><strong>Location (Optional):</strong> To display a city or place name on your photo.</li>
            <li><strong>ATT (Tracking):</strong> For ad personalization consent.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>We use <strong>Google AdMob</strong> to display ads. AdMob may collect:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Advertising Identifier (IDFA), if you consent</li>
            <li>Approximate location from IP address</li>
            <li>Device and OS information</li>
            <li>IP address for fraud prevention</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This information is processed by Google, not by us.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>6. What the App Does NOT Do</h2>
        <p>The app does not:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Upload your photos</li>
            <li>Sell or share data</li>
            <li>Track precise location</li>
            <li>Collect personally identifiable information</li>
            <li>Use analytics SDKs</li>
            <li>Access your social accounts</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>7. GDPR (EU Users)</h2>
        <p>Consent for ads is managed using Apple's ATT framework and Google's UMP system. EU users may manage preferences at any time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>8. CCPA / CPRA</h2>
        <p>RetroN VintageCam does not sell or share personal information. California users may manage advertising data via Google’s privacy dashboard.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>9. CalOPPA</h2>
        <p>This policy is publicly available and will be updated with a new date if changes occur.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>All data stays on your device. Deleting the app removes all stored data.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>11. Children’s Privacy</h2>
        <p>The app is not intended for children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from them.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>12. Security</h2>
        <p>Data is protected by your device’s built-in security such as Face ID, passcode, and sandboxing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>13. Policy Changes</h2>
        <p>If we update this Privacy Policy, we will revise the “Last Updated” date accordingly.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>If you have questions, contact us at:<br />
        <a href="mailto:elifnida@gmail.com">elifnida@gmail.com</a></p>
    </div>

</div>

